"The short stair climbs to the keepers' quarters, the tally-room and the pens."
"Three captives of Tygryth's scattered line sit collared in the pens, the youngest a child."
"The captives have not been fed since the keepers died."
"The captives have stopped wanting, so Alan's sense feels no ripple from them."
"The tally-room holds three hundred years of ledgers: every dragon taken, bled or sold, and to whom."
"The ledgers name where Eira's young were sold, and enter Mari's capture."
